<title>DUBAI: ISLAMIC BANK LENDS LIBYA $66.9 MILLION FOR FARMING.</title>
<headline>ISLAMIC BANK LENDS LIBYA $66.9 MILLION FOR FARMING.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Islamic Development Bank (IDB) on Tuesday signed three agreements extending a $66.9 million soft loan to Libya to finance its farming sector, the acting Libyan ambassador in Saudi Arabia said.</p>
<p>He said the agreements, to develop a fishing port, a flour mill and a fishing farm, were signed in Jeddah.</p>
<p>The Jeddah-based bank was set up in 1975 to promote trade exchanges between Islamic states.</p>
</text>
